Similar to the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA), but for gemini/text links.

Could provide protocol assignments profile of registered gemini/text links URI schemes, ala mailcap: GEMCAP.

data inline
feed inline 
gopher attachment
http attachment
https attachment
mailto attachment
news attachment
tag inline

Nothing prescriptive, but rather normative. A MAY,  RFC wise.

This could provide an organizational principle to the URI space. A guidance. A norm.

GEMCAP could manifest itself as a network accessible, version controlled, gemini/text document maintained by the community.

>From the mailcap introduction, dated September 1993:

"The electronic mail world is in the midst of a transition from
single-part text-only mail to multi-part, multi-media mail.  [...]

