Minor correction:

Titan is a PUT protocol that can send something to a server.  Dioscuri is a
true POST protocol: you send something to the server, and then you get
either a response or an URL pointing to the true response (thanks to the
magic of MIME-type message/external-body).  Dioscuri isn't really intended
as a file-upload protocol, though it could be used that way, but as an
application protocol for requests that won't fit into an URL.  It is in no
way intended for use with forms, but with specialized clients.


