The response has a textual part at time, which is UTF-8 encoded. Assuming a 2x response code,  the content itself is defined by its content-type, which can be anything, in any encoding, following any relevant  convention. UTF-8 (aka Universal Coded Character Set Transformation Format ? 8-bit) itself is an encoding of Unicode. There is no such things as plain text in 2020.

