Hello,

First accessed the internet in 1993, at university. We only had text terminals available when not in class (PCs were not free access). Internet for me at the time was mostly IRC, FTP and email. Didn't know Gopher (still don't!). I was already used to colours, sound, animation (gaming and demoscene on the Atari ST) but text only interfaces did not bother me then, nor do they now.

I like the serenity of Gemini.

I'm tired of the attention grabbing web. I miss the human connection of small sites - because search engines reward those who spend time promoting themselves, small, personal sites have disappeared in the middle of all the noise.

Planning to simplify my own small site, then dual host web and Gemini.

:-)
Alice


