gzip by itself only ever compresses single files, leading to the common .tar.gz combination, where the tape archive (tar) contains any directory structure.

The MIME type text/gemini+gzip has been suggested for this earlier. [1] I think that would be a good solution although it is questionable how well browsers check the MIME type and if they would mistake "text/gemini+gzip" for plain "text/gemini", leading to some confusion. The +gzip suffix is registered by IANA [2].

