There are plenty of guides on the web on how to write HTML and CSS.
JS is not a requirement at all to write them unless you want
interactives, cookies even less so.
=> https://duckduckgo.com/?q=HTML
=> https://duckduckgo.com/?q=CSS

After that you just need hosting, for simple sites something like
http-server is fine, or if you want to make something more robust you
can use apache.
If you don't want to host it yourself there are plenty of ways to pay
for hosting, I haven't done it myself though so I've got no
recommendations.
=> http-server https://github.com/http-party/http-server
=> apache https://httpd.apache.org/
